From 44a4ae1332e3735bec4a5f4f68fa407d76001755 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:00:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Aurora: a window resized on Vulkan keeps its surface and
 keeps drawing

On Linux (X11, NVIDIA) dragging the window's edge lost the surface: Dawn
reports Lost when the swapchain is still out of date after its own rebuild, the
surface was released, and the one made in its place for the same window failed
with VK_ERROR_NATIVE_WINDOW_IN_USE_KHR while the old swapchain still held the
window, losing the device (#325). And while the window was dragged, the picture
grew in steps behind its edges.

- Lost is configured again, as Outdated is, once per configure; only a surface
  lost through 30 configures in a row without a frame is released.
- A Lost or Outdated texture is asked for again, up to twice in the same frame,
  and a suboptimal texture is presented (with one configure after it) rather
  than dropped.
- Vulkan only: at the game's retraces (every 8 ms at most) the window's messages
  are pumped and left queued, and the render worker configures the surface alone
  at the window's newest size before its next texture. The frame buffers keep
  theirs until the resize event, and the present stretches them to the window
  meanwhile. The resize event then configures the surface only if its size
  still differs.
- The first texture of a newly configured surface is not counted as the GPU
  falling behind, which turned Smooth Motion's in-between frames off for 3 s at
  every step of a resize.

Checked on Arch (X11, XFCE, NVIDIA, Vulkan): drag-resizes at 21:9 and 16:9 and
F11 fullscreen switches, hundreds of lost surfaces, all configured again, no
surface released, no crash.
